the-firm-as-one-program-33 : List Word
the-firm-as-one-program-33 = unlines (cons "- **C10** AI researchers at any scale, because their output is checked, not trusted ([P11: A checked construction is trusted no matter who wrote it])." (cons "  Every firm now tries to use AI models for research and engineering and hits the same limit: their output cannot be trusted, so human review is the bottleneck. When a claim is a construction the machine checks, an AI agent's strategy either satisfies the risk invariant or it does not, and its faster hot path either carries its proof or does not ship. The firm can run ten thousand artificial researchers, their output joining the information space as safely as a person's, each building on everything already established. Research capacity stops being a headcount and becomes a compute budget." nil))
